# Master product images.
#
# These five folders hold ~32,000 exported images, about 325 MB. Two reasons
# they stay out of the repository:
#
#   1. Vercel caps a serverless bundle at 250 MB. Committing them fails the
#      deploy -- and the app does not need them, because the catalog the plan
#      generator reads lives in Postgres, not in these files.
#   2. They are exported assets, not source. Git would keep every version of
#      every one of them forever.
#
# The .xlsx workbooks inside these folders ARE tracked, force-added past these
# rules. They are the source of truth the import scripts read and total ~4 MB.
# Once a file is tracked, a gitignore rule no longer applies to it.
#
# Consequence to know: the btl / digital / print / tv browse pages will show
# broken images on a fresh clone and on Vercel. The plan generator is unaffected.
# Cinema, Radio and Transit images were committed before this rule and remain.
src/assets/Masters/btl/
src/assets/Masters/digital/
src/assets/Masters/digital_pr/
src/assets/Masters/print/
src/assets/Masters/tv/

# Generated plans
output/
